{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1396285-idea-for-including-adventure-into-the-cod-city-i-am-doing","id":1396285,"title":"Idea for including Adventure! into the CoD City I am doing","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-06-13T19:44:19-07:00","id":1396285,"title":"Idea for including Adventure! into the CoD City I am doing","content":"So as some of you know I've been writing a looooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooo ooooooooooooooooooooong thing I called The City. Well its still not done .. sorry. But with the lock-down and working at home, I've had many ideas. Some saw the post I did about including in Exalted. So this is one I did bringing in Adventure with a wee bit of Aberrant. I thought of the time period and did this up ... its all still in work in progress and likely might see changes with the newer Continuum stuff on its way.<br /> <br /> Let me know what you think.<br /> <br /> <b>Adventure \u201cDaredevils\u201d of the City<br /> The Pulp Era of the City<br /> <br /> 1900 to 1950</b><br /> The \u201cPulp Era\u201d of the City was a turbulent time. The years leading up to WW1 were seen as a time of growth, of innovation and industrialization of the City. New industry was springing up in Breakwater, bringing hundreds if not thousands of jobs to those willing to do the grunt labor in the factories. New tenements sprung up around the industrial zones, housing the workers and their families. Bars, restaurants, and stores opened in the districts, catering to the working class. With this influx of people, money and business the Gilded Age (1870 to 1900) along with the Industrial Revolution, came to an end, and the Machine age moved well into swing, with new inventions appearing on regular basis as innovation, inspiration and creativity bloomed across the world. Of course with all this new money came new crime. The influx of people looking for jobs was of course larger than the demand, and while some became homeless, others left the city, and still others joined the underworld. Gangs were always looking for new talent. Young or old, everyone had a use in the criminal underworld. The massive influx of manual labor (almost predominately men) led to seedy bars and dance halls which catered to darker tastes, as well as places to imbibe recreational drugs to try to escape the grueling work that was being done. The criminal underworld grew in strength, influencing local establishments, as well as law enforcement and politics.<br /> <br /> When WW1 broke out in July 1914 the US initially stayed out of the conflict, trying to broker peace. The sinking of RMS Lusitania by a German U-boat in May of 1915, causing the death of close to 130 Americans, pushed President Wilson to demand an end to attacks on passenger ships, which Germany did comply with, but Wilson warned repeatedly that the US would not tolerate unrestricted submarine warfare. In January 1917 it was revealed that Germans were resuming unrestricted submarine warfare, as well as planning to aid Mexico in a war on the US to recover territories. By April Germany had sunk seven US merchant ships and the US entered the war.<br /> <br /> Almost three million troops were drafted to send to the warfront, with more sent each day as the year passed till nearly ten thousand a day were being sent by summer 1918.<br /> <br /> The City served as one of the several mustering and shipping points for troops, supplies and equipment till the war ended November 11<sup>th</sup> 1918. It then served as a return port for the both the living and dead as they came home.<br /> <br /> The initial years of what became known as the Interwar Period, (1918 to 1939), was full of opportunities. The inventions used in the war were now being filtered out into the world some good, but many were of more nefarious natures. Science itself, innovation, invention and investigation were at a height though, with people proposing grand ideas of what was to come. Hundreds of inventors scrambled to patent ideas and while some had legitimate ideas, most were not worth mention. In 1922 though, an inventor briefly captured the attention of the scientific community when he unveiled his Telluric Engine. Science had always had a fringe element trying to create things that were out of the pulp novels, serials and radio dramas, from jet packs and rocket cars to spaceships and death rays, the list was expansive as it was fanciful. Some scientists and inventors claimed they had created these things already. Indeed, Verne stated a number of times that Nemo was actually a real person, and that his submarine, the Nautilus, was real.<br /> <br /> Doctor Sir Calvin Hammersmith was a brilliant researcher, who, inspired by Albert Einstein's concepts of space and time, created what was later termed the Hammersmith engine, and invited a number of the wealthy and scientific-minded to a demonstration of his engine. The engine was a device which would, if it worked, extract the &quot;zero-point&quot; energy found in the &quot;emptiness&quot; of space.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, it didn't work.<br /> <br /> The &quot;zero-point&quot; energy \u2014 later understood to be psi and quantum, but called telluric energy by Dr. Hammersmith \u2014 exploded in a great conflagration. The closest attendees were incinerated. Doctor Hammersmith, surviving in the eye of the storm, worked valiantly to save the remaining attendees from destruction. While they escaped, the eye vanished and Doctor Hammersmith himself died.<br /> <br /> The resulting explosion sent a wave front of this energy out across the world, encircling it multiple times and causing strange effects on people, places and things. Reports soon started to trickle in about people with abilities right out of the pulp novels and serials. Explorers reported finding hither to unknown lost cities from legend and myth with entire tribes of people, from amazons to strange beast people. Scientists reported discovering strange new substances like a solution that made wood lighter than air. Reports came from all across the globe of strange new events. All of these had been caused by the burst of \u201ctelluric\u201d energy. Scientist started calling it the Inspired Age, named after the sheer abundance of inspiration that was now occurring.<br /> <br /> Starting in 1922, pulp heroes came to light across the world, springing up in cities, fighting criminals who were exhibiting their own powers and abilities. Some of more famous of these heroes were Maxwell Mercer and his Aeon Society for Gentlemen (consisting of Whitley Styles, Michael Daemon Donighal, Annabelle Lee Newfield, Jake Stefokowski, &quot;Safari&quot; Jack Tallon, and Professor Benjamin Franklin Dixon), Lord Greyfells and his wife Lady Ashe, the Aviator, the Whisperer, and Defender. Villains of equal repute also came onto the scene, like the King of the World, The Master of the Air, The Ubiquitous Dragon, the Jade Eye, King Thunder and the Wraith. For the years until the outbreak of World War 2, these heroes fought, explored and adventured around the globe and The City was no different. With its own collection of pulp heroes and villains, prohibition in full swing, and several years till the Great Depression, the City and indeed the world, was a place of wonder, adventure and innovation. It was an inspired time.<br /> <br /> When the Great Depression hit, the impoverished leaned heavily on the stories of the heroes, the adventurers and inventors, their exploits and tales giving them hope in the hard times. The lean years caused strife in the big cities, and The City was no different. Riots over food and squalid conditions in the slums and ghettos led to increased criminal activity.<br /> <br /> When World War 2 broke out it brought a general end to the Great Depression as millions were drafted and sent war and millions more were employed to make arms, ammo, equipment and other materials for the war effort. The pulp heroes either faded away at this time or went to war with their respective fellow soldiers, either in costume or as everyday men in the field. Some were well known on the war front, such as Defender, the Aviator, Sunstrike, and the Tank on the Allied side, and the Iron Eagle, Annihilator, Ghost Legion, and Scythe on the Axis, to name a few. After the war, those that had survived returned to a different world. With the advent of the Cold War, most of the pulp heroes faded into memory. Some tried to continue their work, but were either killed or arrested. The last of the great pulp heroes disappeared in 1949, doing battle with his nemesis on the top of the Sears Tower in New York City. The final battle found the villain dead on the observation deck the hero gone, never seen again. Of note was also the fading of \u201cunknown places\u201d. Adventurers and explorers were no longer reporting that they were finding lost cities, tribes, countries and islands. Indeed even the ones found had become lost again, the routes to them no longer seeming to connect anymore, the coordinates on the map leading to somewhere else and locals no longer remembering they even existed. It was like the world suddenly forgot the pulp age had occurred except as stories, movies, and radio dramas.<br /> <br /> Some researchers note that the reason for this was that the wave of Telluric energy had dissipated to the point where it no longer influenced the way the world was. Other theorized that humanity had moved beyond the need those heroes. Still others whispered that things in the dark shadows of the world, things best not named, had done their best to remove the influence of these heroes from the world in order to preserve their place in it.<br /> <br /> <b>Supernaturals in the War Years and Pulp Age of the Inspired</b><br /> <b>Kindred</b> \u2013 The European kindred were severely decimated, with hundreds, if not thousands of them killed in both WW1 and WW2 due to the damage done by bombings, gas attacks, shelling and other attacks. Many Kindred never knew what hit them, as a bomb or shell would hit the building they were sleeping in during the day. Others starved, as their hunting grounds were decimated and the people ran for safe zones and other adapted, like the Caporetti and Brothers of Ypres. American Kindred fared better of course as the bombs were not dropping there, but the loss of large portions of their herd did cause some princes to put restrictions on feeding in place. WW2 cause even more restrictions for North America kindred, with some even taking civilian jobs on bases as night workers to feed on the massive amount of troops training there. The appearance of the Inspired didn\u2019t affect the Kindred that much. Some of the more overt of their kind found themselves targeted by heroes not realizing what they were hunting, with a few being killed by the heroes. Some heroes upon discovering vampires were real took it upon themselves to hunt down and destroy them, like Blackstaff, who plagued the Kindred of Atlanta for close to three years, each time they thought they had killed him, he would show up at the most inopportune time to spoil whatever plan they were putting into motion or Ravager, who scoured the ruins of Germany post WW2 hunting Kindred in an effort to locate the one who had killed his wife and children. The lost places appearing out of the mists of legend, myth and story, did throw the Kindred for a loop, especially when such places as the ruins of the Camarilla tunnels under Rome, the dead city of Kaymakli where it is said an entire clan of Kindred were massacred in one night, and Nosgoth, a mythical ancient city where vampires ruled openly, were rediscovered out of the blue. The other places that came to light put hundreds of artifacts in play across the world as well, and Kindred, especially those of the Ordo Dracul and Circle of the Crone sent out agents to secure these artifacts as well as figuring out ways to travel to the locales themselves, indeed it is said there were no less than twenty tramp steamers on the seas that where basically mobile havens for powerful Kindred, not to mention the RMS Abyss and RMS Harbinger, luxury liners that catered to Kindred, ferrying them across the oceans of the world. When the lost places began to fade, the Kindred made a final mad scramble to get anything they could. A large group of Ordo Dracul were lost when the routes to Nosgoth vanished, though in the 2000s there has been rumors of strange Kindred appearing bearing unknown relics and artifacts, offering them for money and information.<br /> <br /> <b>Forsaken</b> \u2013 Werewolves can fit in easily, so the tumultuous war years did not affect them that badly. Many Forsaken and their kin were drafted into both wars, especially WW2, and many died overseas, as even Forsaken aren\u2019t immune to shelling, gas, bombs and bullets when they are used in such force. Some Pure reveled in the war, indeed there was an entire SS squad comprised of Pure during WW2 who operated as a covert strike team across Europe and into Russia known as the Blitzwolfe. The Inspired did little to beleaguer the Forsaken. Those few heroes who ran across them in their non-human forms either ran or put a brave fight. There were some heroes who could take a Forsaken when it came down to it, the Blitzwolfe unit was wiped out by the heroic efforts of The Tank, the \u201cRussian Living Weapon\u201d, but on a whole the Forsaken generally interacted little with the Inspired. The resurgence of lost places similarly did little to them, though the tales of someone finding lost Pangea in the center of the earth did cause a few to go looking. Forsaken adventurers and explorers did wander some of the newly found lost lands, but apart from some artifacts, they had little do with them.<br /> <br /> <b>The Lost</b> \u2013 Changelings suffered during the war years. Living with the rest of humanity, side by side in most cases meant when the bombs, shells and bullets came they were killed just like everyone else. They were drafted like everyone else, worked the factories like everyone else, and suffered like everyone else. The Lost suffered the hardest in Germany when their nature was discovered by members of the SS. Special hunting squads were sent out to find Changelings in order to catch them. Those that were caught were sent to a special base in the mountains, never to be seen again. The rise of the Inspired did little for the Lost. Changelings couldn\u2019t benefit from the energies and most heroes and villains had no clue the Lost even existed. The appearance of lost places intrigued the Lost and many took trips to explore them, bringing back artifacts and treasures from the lost locales.<br /> <br /> <b>The Awakened</b> \u2013 Mages are outwardly no different than an ordinary mortal. During both World Wars, mages did indeed find themselves being drafted to serve on one side or the other. In the first war, it was mostly European mages who were occasionally drafted and brought into the conflict. Most did their best to avoid the conflict, but there were those on either side who used the war to further their own goals. After WW1, the Thule Society was founded. This group was rife with awakened who sought to further their own power and it was their doing that pushed the Society to back the Deutsche Arbeiterpartei, who would become the Nazi party. The awakened of the Axis sought to win the war and spread their puppet regime across the world. They saw the Axis as way to re-usher in the age of enlightenment. Of course other members of the Thule Society saw it as a way to open the world to their dark gods in a bid for power of their own, while still others wanted the power they saw the Axis had as a way to further their own paths on the world. Awakened on the Allies side were largely ungrouped, unlike the Axis, and so suffered from a number of setbacks till finally a core group gathered and formed a cabal known as the Spear. Co-operation between the five paths and orders was unprecedented during WW2 once the Spear formed, as they strove to stop the various plans of the Axis awakened. The emergence of the Inspired after WW1 cause quiet a number to begin research into telluric energy. The appearance of so-called lost worlds and places, sent dozens of awakened, both Axis and Allies, on expeditions to capture artifacts of power. Some rumors persist that when the Axis awakened noted they were going to lose, they used their powers to establish a safe haven in one of the lost places for the elite of their order along with families, servants and those of the Nazis that had served them. After the lost places faded rumors of a lost Nazi colony persisted with it being linked too many different places, such as in Inner Earth, the dark side of the moon, Antarctica, even a lost continent in the Pacific Ocean.<br /> <br /> <b>The Created</b> \u2013 Prometheans suffered in WW1, especially in Europe. The trenches and the use of gas saw (check source book as I remember there being something about ww1 and mass graves of people being used to create prometheans). The intervening years saw them go into hiding, with many succumbing to PTSD due to the horrors they saw. WW2 equally saw death and destruction of those in the theatres of war and the Nazis were known to be experimenting with raising the dead, creating (clones?? Check book). The Inspired and the Created rarely dealt with each other and those chance encounters were generally brushed off. The lost lands interestingly gave the Created something to try to reach. These places were devoid of people and pandorans, and they might hold secrets to help them on their paths. Many Created attempted journey\u2019s to these places. Few if any returned.<br /> <br /> <b>The Unchained</b> \u2013 No one knows what the God Machine thought of the World Wars. Some posit that they were carefully arranged by the God Machine in order to facilitate some plan, possible in response to over population or something. Others have theorized that the two wars were mistakes in the system, that the God Machine did not want either of them to happen. No one is really sure. When the telluric engine exploded and sent the shockwave of telluric energy around the world the God Machine took notice though. Angels long dormant sprung to life in a panicked state. Infrastructures long thought dead suddenly sprung to life and the Unchained went on the war path all of a sudden. When hidden and lost places became findable again, Unchained immediately set out to them to search them, with the God Machines agents not far behind. Some posit that the slow decline of telluric energy and it eventual diminishment to a non-measurable source just into the 1950s was due to the God Machine. Most Inspired never encountered agents of the God Machine nor the rebellious kin, the Unchained. Those few that did were either killed or taken by the God Machine\u2019s Angels to be \u201cexamined\u201d.<br /> <br /> <b>The Unbound</b> \u2013 Sin Eaters were much in demand across the world in WW1, the intervening years and WW2. The number of unquiet ghosts created by the two wars and the great depression kept these enigmatic people very busy. Those few Unbound that served in the wars often spent their time trying to deal with the dead, while other tried to keep the cenotes closed as there was the threat of surge that would blow open the gates into the underworld, causing ghosts to spill out into the world. There are no recorded interactions between Inspired and the Unbound, though most Inspired would probably just take them for a spirit medium of some type. The appearance of lost worlds intrigued a number of the Unbound and some ventured forth to explore them. Some returned, others did not. Those that did reported the ghosts of the places strange, lost in time and whispering of powerful, dark beings prowling the underworld looking something.<br /> <br /> <b>The Vigil</b> \u2013 The Vigil is largely made up of mortals, though some are gifted with a bit of extra stuff. The war years saw thousands of people involved with the various compacts and conspiracies involved in the conflicts. For several of the larger more global conspiracies the war years saw both loss and growth, with some profited extremely well, such as the Chieron Group. For most of the Vigil, the Inspired were seen as heroes. Normal people who took upon themselves to fight the darkness and what lay within it. Some of the larger groups, like the Chieron Group, were interested in what made the Inspired what they were, and a number of these people were \u201crecruited\u201d by some of the various compacts and conspiracies. The sudden appearance of lost place had agents of the larger groups scrambling in teams to explore them.<br /> <br /> <b>The Arisen</b> \u2013 Arisen plans involve decades if not centuries of planning, easily rivaling the kindred and God Machine in their intricate complexity. For the Arisen the War Years passed largely without incident, at least for those not in the Middle East and Europe. A number lost their cults and their homes in the bombings and the invasions. Several had their artifacts and treasures stolen by thieves Axis and Allied alike in the tumult of the war, with the Thule Society especially interested in anything they could find. The Inspired had little to no contact with the Arisen, though some did deal with their cults on and off. The lost places were of immense interest to the Arisen and many sent their cultists to these places to retrieve whatever they could.<br /> <br /> <b>The Begotten</b> \u2013 Perhaps one of the stranger of the supernaturals, Begotten were caught off guard by both world wars. Draft notices took several to the army. For some of them it was a buffet, but for others is was starvation, and when deployed into remote areas it only got worse. Stories about lone squads losing their minds and going mad, attacking their own or anyone who came near them, cropped up here and there, as well as stories of strange dead villages where everyone had died of fright or worse. The Begotten of Europe suffered greatly in the conflicts, especially with the Nazis, though rumors persist of a Begotten who reveled in his place as a commandant of one of the infamous camps. The Inspired were noticed by the Begotten but largely lumped in with other mortals. The few that encountered one generally found that they were sometimes a little harder to influence and stalk, but like any other mortal, they had fears, dreams and hope that could be preyed on, indeed some were incredibly full of themselves with their abilities making them prime targets occasionally. The lost lands drew interest from some of the begotten, but largely they left those places alone.<br /> <br /> <b>The Remade</b> \u2013 The Remade saw a surge in their numbers during the war years. From both Allied and Axis plans to create super soldiers, to resistance fighters seeking ways to beat the invaders, to those poor unfortunates in the camps who were selected to be tested on. The Inspired and the Remade didn\u2019t really interact much and in those rare cases when they did, it was usually with one thinking the other was of the same ilk. Indeed a few of the Remade joined in with the Pulp heroes to fight evil. The various lost places were interestingly enough, the source for a number of new Remade. Whispers of strange labs in forgotten countries and research on lost islands, as well as lost races of man and even underground empires of advanced technology were heard as the possible source for the Remade.<br /> <br /> <br /> I will post write ups on the people mentioned.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":722,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/722-walksforever","user":"Walksforever","date":". 06-14-2020, 07:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/722-walksforever","name":"Walksforever","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar722_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"213"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-14T16:46:04-07:00","id":1396523,"title":"","content":"<b>Inspired People of Note:</b><br /> <br /> <b>Pre WW2 (1922-1939)</b><br /> <b>Blackstaff \u2013 </b>No one is quiet sure who Blackstaff was. He appeared on the scene in 1924 in Atlanta, dressed all in black and grey, with a sharpened staff of black wood. No one was quite sure who it was he was going up against at night, but when the first couple of ash piles were discovered in the areas he was seen, those in the know, figured it out. Hunting kindred is never an easy task. Even an Inspired will find it a difficult task, as while the younger ones are only a little more powerful than an average human, the older ones are not only physically more powerful, but possess mystical abilities that can turn even the strongest of minds to paste. Blackstaff seemed to be able to hold his own against the Kindred he fought. He survived till his disappearance in 1928, while on the path of an older kindred, his body was never found.<br /> <br /> Of course at this point we should note the people from Adventure! Benjamin Franklin Dixon, Michael Daemon Donighal, Calvin Hammersmith, Maxwell Anderson Mercer, Michael Maxwell Mercer, Annabelle Lee Newfield, Scalper Dutch, Jake Stefokowski, Whitley Styles, Jack Tallon, King of the World, Ubiquitous Dragon, Doctor Zorbo, Machinatrix, Mister Saturday, The Czar, Uriah Stafford. To see who these people were, you'll need to snag a copy of Adventure!<br /> <br /> <b>City Inspired of Note</b><br /> I will post these a bit at time .. starting with the two figures who were basically the &quot;poster children&quot; for the inspired in the city. Lord Greyfell and Lady Ashe. <br /> <br /> <b>City Inspired of Note</b><br /> <b>Lord Greyfells </b>\u2013 Lord John Gordon was born the third son of the Baron Greyfells, a small almost non-existent Barony in the middle of England. With two older brothers, he would never inherit the title and instead applied his talents to the arts of science, finance and deduction as he grew up, excelling at school. He left for the war when it broke out in 1914, serving as a lieutenant and advancing to the rank of major by the war\u2019s end. Taking his contacts from the war and playing the now recovering markets, he amassed a sizable fortune, becoming quite rich by the time he turned 25, sizably more than his father and two older siblings combined, something that drove a wedge between them when they required his assistance to bring their ancestral estate out of debt due to their mismanagement. After bailing out the estate and setting up a trust that would keep it afloat, another wedge, he left for the Americas, settling in the City in 1918. <br /> <br /> He met his wife a year after his arrival, courting her for six months before proposing. The two were married and took up residence on an estate on Glenn Ross Island in 1922. The solved their first crime literally by accident two years later, when they read about a theft of various art treasures in the city that was confusing the local police. They managed to figure out who was doing it and got a taste for sleuthing. Applying their resources and considerable talents they took to being consulting detectives, like Sherlock Holmes and Dr. Watson, becoming noted celebrities in 1925 after solving a case involving the kidnapping of three young children. The two continued to solve crimes big and small, as well as thwart criminal masterminds like King Thunder, The Jade Eye, The Gentleman\u2019s Gentleman and Wraith. The two also delved into supernatural mysteries, coming into contact with a number of the City\u2019s supernatural species over the course of their investigations. Greyfells\u2019s own occult knowledge was considered quite formidable, easily rivaling some of the Ordo Dracul and Awakened.<br /> <br /> One of Greyfells and his wife\u2019s biggest success was when they apprehended King Thunder after a lengthy case. The final pitched battle between Greyfells and Thunder became legend and has had many stories, TV shows and even a couple movies done about it. Convicted on multiple counts ranging from murder to larceny, King Thunder was sentenced to Asher Island Penitentiary for with a triple life sentence to be served consecutively.<br /> <br /> Greyfells spent the Second World War working for military intelligence, travelling to Washington DC frequently to work with the joint chiefs. He was instrumental in assisting in several scientists escape from Germany during and at the end of the war. Post war, he returned to doing consulting with the local law enforcement. He however found that the thrill of the investigations were not what they used to be, and spent more and more of his time studying books of esoteric knowledge he\u2019d accumulated over the years.<br /> Heeding a call to Washington DC, Greyfells rejoined the Intelligence community working towards founding an external intelligence group to help defend American interests. Once the nascent CIA was up and running he finally decided it was time to stop and write his memoirs and retired to Glenn Ross Island to write and take care of his ailing wife, who passed away 1964 from cancer.<br /> <br /> Greyfells faded from the public eye, the pulp era and the criminal masterminds he once did battle with now gone, dead or in prison. Little was heard about Gretfells till a break in at his estate in 1968 when he surprisingly and easily took down three young men, even though he was just into his 70s. With his name in the news once again, interest in his life reemerged and he was again the subject of stories and a movie. He spoke at the local schools and was often invited to major social engagements. The police even went to him with difficult cases to get his perspective. Greyfells published his memoirs finally, watching as they rocketed to the top of the best sellers list and was approached with yet more movie and tv deals which he politely declined.<br /> <br /> 1995 saw a large celebration on Glenn Ross Island for their oldest resident, Lord Greyfells, who turned 100. Greyfells, confined to a wheelchair, but still in good health, led multiple tours of his house to friends, showing off his collection of pulp history memorabilia as well as his famous case note files. A statue of his wife and him was unveiled at the local park near his mansion. Greyfells\u2019s health deteriorated after this, age and his life finally catching up with him. He spent his remaining years doing research and preparation and final passed away in his sleep at the age of 103 on a chilly March afternoon in 1998. His house was opened as a museum to his and his wife\u2019s work, and saw hundreds visit it each day for the next few years. The estate approved a TV series biography of his life and adventures and a series of movies of his more fantastical pulp action adventures was also commissioned.<br /> <br /> Greyfells and his wife are folk heroes, often quoted as what people should strive to be like in life. Some whisper that Greyfells didn\u2019t die, that he still lives in his mansion, hidden away. Others say his ghost haunts the mansion and all his works. <br /> <br /> There are several scholarships named after him at both Edwards University and the City College, as well as the Greyfells Foundation, which seeks to help the less fortunate. Several parks, buildings and one major road are named after him and his wife.<br /> <br /> <i>The Shadows</i> \u2013 Greyfells was a Daredevil, empowered by the strange telluric energies that were released in the early 1900s. He possessed genius level intelligence and deductive reasoning along with an eidetic memory. His physical abilities were also enhanced, possessing Olympic caliber training in running, lifting, boxing, and wrestling. He was basically Batman without the costume, and angst.<br /> <br /> <i>Appearance</i> \u2013 The most common pictures of Greyfells from his prime show him as a tall man with jet black hair cut short, a mustache, goatee, and blue eyes. He was considered handsome and was in excellent physical shape. He was said to have a deep voice with a Yorkshire accent, clean spoken and always friendly and polite to anyone regardless of station. <br /> <br /> <b>Lady Ashe</b> \u2013 Helen Gloria Ashe was born in the City, the daughter of a wealthy family who owned multiple industrial businesses. Unlike her sisters, she was not happy with the thought of being paraded about till the right man saw her and asked for her parent\u2019s permission to marry her so he could secure a dynasty for himself. She busied herself with studies of math, science, and philosophy, easily completing courses and excelling in the subjects. She entered the medical field at 19, having decided to study to be a doctor. <br /> <br /> She met Greyfells at her family\u2019s annual Christmas party. She liked to recall that she looked up over a glass of wine across the room and right into his blue eyes and that was that. She knew that he was the one. She remembered dancing with him all night after that and the tender proposal he made six months later.<br /> <br /> Ashe was the one to bring their first case to their attention and from then on the two of them were inseparable as they did their investigations. Ashe\u2019s medical and scientific knowledge mixed with Greyfells\u2019s memory, deductive reason and physical presence made a formidable pair.<br /> <br /> Over the years of their work Ashe became the belle of the City, with many seeing her as the perfect example of what it was to be a modern woman, strong, intelligent, and able to handle herself as an equal to her husband in all aspects, and while there were those that derided her avant-garde nature, the populace love her. <br /> <br /> When Greyfells went to work for the government, Ashe stayed in the City, helping at the local hospitals while raising their children and doing a bit of consulting when needed in medical issues for the police. In the intervening years before Greyfells went back to help found the CIA, the two began to draft their memoirs of their times and adventures.<br /> <br /> It was a year after Greyfells had begun the work with the nascent CIA that she was diagnosed with cancer. Restricted to a wheelchair a year later she nevertheless kept up her work with the local hospitals and charities, helping whenever she could. She finally succumbed to the disease in 1964, at the age of 64 years, passing in her sleep with family present.<br /> <br /> The City mourned her loss. She had been considered the figurehead of the City, with her silhouette and picture having been used by many for ads for various city projects, especially the social season ones. Her name alone would attract the elite to gatherings and the masses to events where she was appearing. Her death came as a blow to all. The City took a day to mourn, the passage of her body marked by a massive cavalcade through the city with National Guard and police escorts to the cemetery where she was interred into a large mausoleum. Thousands thronged the cemetery as hundreds stood with Greyfells as he said goodbye to his wife. <br /> <br /> Every year since her death hundreds had laid wreaths at the tomb on the anniversary of her death, and after the statue of her and Greyfells was unveiled they laid them there as well. Multiple books, tv shows and three movies have been done of her life. There are several scholarships at both the college and university that hold her name, as well as dozens of parks, a river, buildings, a bridge, and a roadway. Her image is seen daily on several billboards, used to promote various social causes, from homelessness to literacy.<br /> <br /> <i>The Shadows </i>\u2013 Helen was also a Daredevil. Like her husband she possessed genius level intelligence and memory along with skills in the medical fields that out stripped all in the City. Like her husband she was in prime physical shape, having trained extensively in ballet, formal dance, horseback riding and gymnastics.<br /> <br /> <i>Appearance </i>\u2013 Helen was a classic beauty with fiery red hair that shone in the sun like liquid fire. She was trim and athletic due to a healthy lifestyle with plenty of exercise. She was kind, soft spoken and friendly to everyone.<br /> <br /> Yes, I know, they are basically Holmes and Watson... but I did that on purpose, cause we all need a little Baker Street in our lives .. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/722-walksforever","name":"Walksforever","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar722_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"213"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-16T06:43:31-07:00","id":1396857,"title":"","content":"Alright, couple more.<br /> <br /> <b>King Thunder</b> \u2013 Born Edward Simon Whitney, the man who would one day be King Thunder was the fifth child of a devoutly religious family, where his father was partial to the passage of \u201cspare the rod and spoil the child\u201d. Beaten for any infraction that his parents think they saw, Edward grew up bitter, angry and wanting nothing more than to escape his parents. He went to work in a factory at 14 under orders of his father in order to pay his way, giving all wages to his parents, who would beat him if they suspected he was keeping something back. It was in the factory that he came into his nickname of King Thunder.<br /> <br /> Always a larger child, working the factory brought his muscles out, and by the time he was 16 he was massively muscled, swinging a huge hammer to destroy rubble in the wreckers part of the factory. It was on a Tuesday that the name was given him, when he swung the hammer and a metal rebar in the concrete cause it to reverberate across the entire yard and through simple luck caused the entire concrete section to shatter and crumble in a massive roar of thunder like noise. Standing there as the dust cloud clear, stripped to the waist showing his muscles, the light caught him just right and people noted he looked like a king. Considering the thundering noise that had just occurred they called him King Thunder for fun. It stuck and Edward capitalized on it. By the time he reached 20 he was working as a low level enforcer for a local gang, prized for his ability to do huge amounts of damage if needed. What they didn\u2019t know was that he was applying a keen mind to learn the ways of the gang and how it worked. Three years later he was running the gang. Two years after that he was running all the gangs in his area behind the scenes, a hidden crime boss. On his 30<sup>th</sup> birthday he consolidated the entire factory area and dockside gangs under his control, crowning himself King Thunder for real. He gifted himself with his parents brought to him and watching as they prostrated themselves before him, trembling with fear. It is said he sentenced them to a punishment like the one they visited on him all his growing years and had the hauled off to a secret location where their every action could be met with a severe beating done by several of his men done at the whim of the men on how they felt about the action. It is said his parents lasted two years and that King Thunder administered the fatal beatings himself in the end.<br /> <br /> King Thunder ran afoul of Lord Greyfells and Lady Ashe two years after his consolidation of the gangs. The two heroes managed to bring down one of his gang leaders and splinter the gang itself during an investigation. Thunder did his best to try to get the goods on the two, but they were New City elite and he was Old City crime, and the paths they walked were very different. He attempted to have them \u201cpersuaded\u201d to leave his affairs alone but this just made them look closer. He attempted to kidnap Lady Ashe as leverage, but sadly all that did was cause Lord Greyfells to concentrate all his efforts on taking Thunder down. Things finally came to a head late one afternoon in July 1937 when Lord Greyfells and Lady Ashe managed to corner Thunder at his base of operations. With the police coming in behind them the two managed to get into Thunder\u2019s inner sanctum where they fought with him for several minutes before the police managed to also gain entrance and surround them. Thunder was taken into custody.<br /> <br /> In August he was convicted of murder, racketeering, bribery, extortion, and a dozen other crimes. He was sent to Asher Island Penitentiary to serve three consecutive life sentences.<br /> Now the thing about Asher Island Maximum Penitentiary is that it was controlled by a member of the Kindred called Kingsmere, who found the old lair of the imprisoned Begotten beneath it and then proceeded to enslave the trapped thing to do his bidding. Kingsmere used it to torture the dreams of the inmates, especially the lifers doing hard time. He then fed off those people after he charted their behaviors for his studies. Edward became a personal project for Kingsmere after his arrival and spent the next 18 years being subjected to the hunger of the Begotten as well as being a both a food and research source. It broke him in more ways than one. Reduced to a shell of what he once was, Edward turned to God, becoming a model prisoner for his time. He prayed all the time, ran prayer meetings, held services, all hoping that the nightmares would fade and that Satan would stop visiting him. It didn\u2019t, but the change in behavior, something the prison psychologist confirmed, got him an early release as a parolee. The man that exited the prison that cold February morning was emaciated, grey haired, twitchy and paranoid, constantly whispering prayers under his breath. With the help of his parole officer he got a job as a stock boy for a pittance while living in a tiny little apartment in a run-down area of town<br /> <br /> Though he was no longer under the sway of the begotten or Kingsmere the damage done was irreversible. Edward turned to heroin to try to help him sleep at night, eventually overdosing to stop the nightmares and flashbacks. His body was found in 1964 and he was buried in a pauper\u2019s unmarked grave in a low class cemetery on the same day that the City mourned Lady Ashe.<br /> <br /> <i>The Shadows</i> \u2013 King Thunder was gifted with enhanced strength and stamina, as well as an almost sixth sense for things about to go wrong.<br /> <br /> <i>Appearance</i> \u2013 Before he went to prison, King Thunder was nearly 7ft tall and built like a body builder, yet he moved easily, comfortable with his size and weight. Salt and pepper colored short hair with a perpetual three days growth of beard, he looked like he\u2019d been through his share of fights, with a misshapen nose, deep brown eyes and one ear slightly deformed. <br /> <br /> <b>The Jade Eye</b> \u2013 Kai Wu \u2013 A crime lord and frequent nemesis of the Whisperer in Old City. Kai was born into power, the first son of a prominent underworld family in China Town, where he was groomed to succeed his father as leader of the tong the family controlled. Trained in various martial arts, as well as tutored in academia, he became the single minded and powerful leader of the tong upon his father\u2019s death.<br /> <br /> Kai wasn\u2019t known as the Jade Eye at this time, he was just another tong leader, one of several in the area. A chance encounter with the Whisperer lead him to realize that there was something more to the world. Using the resources at hand he had his people buy and steal dozens of so called mystical artifacts in an attempt to find one that might gift him with power so he could deal with the Whisperer. A chance would have it one of the various items turned out to have been imbued with telluric energy and when he opened and breathed in the fumes inside it, it infused him as well. The most noticeable effect was his eyes becoming a luminous jade green in color, something he took to hiding with dark glasses. The other effects were increased manual dexterity, stamina, strength and intelligence. Kai went about consolidating the tongs in his area, forming a single powerful tong. Known now as The Jade Eye, he ruled the China Town area\u2019s underworld with an iron fist. Those that resisted faced his master level martial arts combined with his increased physical powers, making him a powerful foe. His next encounter with the Whisperer came late one night as he oversaw a shipment of heroin being brought in. The two grappled and fought while the tong hastily collected the drugs and The Whisperer lost the fight, disappearing into the darkness. This emboldened the Jade Eye who doubled his efforts in the underworld, seeing having a free reign due to beating the Whisperer. Of course this wasn\u2019t so, as instead the Whisperer merely took a different tack to his tactics, striking at small targets and small groups of tong, whittling away at the Jade Eye\u2019s operations, damaging his cash flow and causing his people to doubt his leadership.<br /> <br /> Having had enough of this, the Jade Eye used his contacts in the police to get them to declare the Whisperer a public enemy and a get a manhunt started. At the same time he put a bounty on the Whisperer, figuring one way or another he would be rid of the pest. Sadly all this did was cause the Whisperer to not only become even more wraithlike in his operations, but one night three weeks after the manhunt, the Jade Eye woke to find the Whisperer sitting in a chair in front of his bed, wanting to talk. It is not known what was discussed, only that the Jade Eye canceled the bounty and used his influence to call off the manhunt the next day. Rumors persist that the three young women who were sharing the Jade Eye\u2019s bed that night all went insane after seeing the Whisperer.<br /> <br /> The Jade Eye continued his operations slowly and with less fervor, having to always wonder if the Whisperer or Lord Greyfells or even The City\u2019s newest crime fighter, The Aviator, might interfere with his people. Over the course of five years he worked on and off with other crime lords like King Thunder and the Silent Lady in order to try to remove the heroes who opposed them, but were always at an impasse in the end. Finally having had enough of his longtime nemesis, the Jade Eye called in a hero hunter known as the Judge from New York to track down and kill the Whisperer.<br /> <br /> It took three years for Judge to finally find the Whisperer\u2019s lair, located in the railyards in Breakwater Industrial Park. This led to a final confrontation between the three people. The fight itself went badly for the Judge and Jade Eye, as the Whisperer had grown more powerful over the years. In a final act of willpower, the Jade Eye channeled the telluric energy in his body into a powerful strike which counter acted with the power the Whisperer was wielding. The resulting explosion killed both the Jade Eye and the Judge and left the Whisperer amnesiac, wandering off into Old City. The tong splintered without his leadership, fracturing back into multiple small gangs fighting over territory and other petty disputes. The bodies of the Jade Eye and Judge were taken and buried in unmarked graves in one of Old City\u2019s cemeteries.<br /> <br /> <i>The Shadows</i> \u2013 The Jade Eye was already in top physical and mental shape, having been trained to run the tong almost from birth. His martial art skills were master class and his academia were easily in the top percentile for those in the City. The telluric energy he absorbed gave him several benefits. Increased speed, stamina, hand-eye co-ordination, and heightened perception. He also gained the ability to channel the telluric energy in him into his strikes, causing his hands or feet to glow green when he struck. Using this would deplete his energy, so he did it infrequently, but it caused his strikes to feel like being hit by a truck. <br /> <br /> <i>Appearance </i>\u2013 Kai was of average appearance, indeed, some say he was rather homely overall. Dark hair and eyes, a slightly too big nose and slightly shorter than average, Kai did not cut an impressive figure, but he made up for it in his sheer presence of personality, which was that of a true overlord. His stern deep voice and razor wit easily overrode any problems his appearance had.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/722-walksforever","name":"Walksforever","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar722_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"213"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-16T08:00:32-07:00","id":1396871,"title":"","content":"This is great! I love Lord Greyfells and Lady Ashe. Also the reference to Kaymakli.<br /> <br /> What if the God-Machine was either built by the Doyen or allied with the Doyen?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-16T15:52:09-07:00","id":1396964,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1396285-idea-for-including-adventure-into-the-cod-city-i-am-doing?p=1396871#post1396871\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is great! I love Lord Greyfells and Lady Ashe. Also the reference to Kaymakli.<br /> <br /> What if the God-Machine was either built by the Doyen or allied with the Doyen?</div> </div> </div> </div>I tend to go with the whole idea that the God Machine didn't like the telluric energies that occurred and that it was drained away by God Machine nodes, structures and sites. The appearance of the nova/aberrant i think it likely saw as another aberration, and probably helped in mankind developing psions Think of a world of &quot;mental man&quot;, almost all who go through a prometheus chamber to strengthen their abilities (and have God Machine nanites put in) which allows the God Machine to link to all of them former a massive unconscious hive mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/722-walksforever","name":"Walksforever","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar722_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"213"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-16T18:43:46-07:00","id":1396983,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/722-walksforever\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar722_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"722\" data-vbnamecard=\"722\">Walksforever</a> I love it!<br /> <br /> You could still tie the God-Machine into the Doyen if you wanted though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-17T06:15:00-07:00","id":1397074,"title":"","content":"Next couple of the City's Pulp Era heroes/villians.<br /> <br /> <b>The Silent Lady</b> \u2013 Not much is known of this strange villainess who appeared on the scene one day as the architect behind a series of bold murders of rich men. Known also as the Silent Widow, the Black Death and even Death\u2019s Mistress, she preyed on rich men, young and old. Her victims were found dead of natural causes, usually a heart attack or aneurism, always in bed and always in the morning after a night of \u201cromance\u201d. While the doctors weren\u2019t quite ready to say it, the general theory was that she was somehow killing them with sex. She was on the front page of the paper when her current husband, a wealthy young man whose parents were among the elite of the City, died a month after they were married. She caught the attention of Lord Greyfells who did some digging and found the trail of dead husbands. The police of course couldn\u2019t arrest her as there was no proof she did anything wrong, though the family did sue for wrongful death, something they lost as the Silent Lady had lawyers who were very well paid and very good. <br /> <br /> Greyfells\u2019s research found six dead men, in the US and Canada at least, and possibly others down into Central and South America, stretching down to Argentina. His investigations discovered that some of the deaths stretched back decades, which was interesting considering she looked to be in her early to mid-30s. His investigations soon revealed that she tended to burn through the money she got, buying expensive gifts and throwing lavish parties. He brought her past to light and the police dug deeper, discovering possible connections to other murder investigations, none of which could be proven. <br /> <br /> The Silent Lady became a femme fatale for Greyfells, constantly being found in the middle of his investigations when they involved the rich and famous and elite of the City. She constantly attempted to seduce him, but Greyfells\u2019s loyalty to his wife was strong, though many wondered if perhaps he had sampled her offer. <br /> The Silent Lady worked on and off as an \u201cunwitting\u201d front \u201cman\u201d to various crime lords, always claiming and managing to prove that she didn\u2019t know they were behind the venture she was dealing with. The police of course got very tired of this occurring over and over and eventually with Greyfells and the Aviator\u2019s help, managed to catch her on something that could be prosecuted. Convicted and sentenced to five years, the Silent Lady got out of prison within a year for good behavior and quietly dropped off the scene. Rumors of her still in the City would surface here and there, but most claimed that she\u2019d sailed to Europe.<br /> It wasn\u2019t until Greyfells\u2019s 101<sup>st</sup> year that she re-appeared, looking as young as ever. She sat, had a quiet drink with him, kissed him to remind him of what he\u2019d never sampled, and then left. Careful examination of the photos during his funeral by Stormcaller have revealed her in them, standing in the forefront with other mourners. She also appears in photos of Lady Ashe\u2019s funeral. In all of them she looks to be in her early 30s, not having aged a day.<br /> <br /> <i>The Shadows </i>\u2013 The Silent Lady is cursed with a type of vampirism, where she feeds slowly off the life force of the people around her with intense emotions, the more powerful and intense the more delicious. For her the best occur during the acts of romance and passion, especially sex. The downside is that if she lefts herself go she can literally kill her mate by draining him dry, causing a cardiac event or aneurism. She can\u2019t control this which is why she has left a string of dead husbands across the world. Of course the side effect is that she\u2019s perpetually young.<br /> <br /> <i>Appearance</i> \u2013 A stunning woman of Latin American descent, with long dark hair and a willowy figure. She always dressed to accentuate her figure, making sure that whenever she entered a room all eyes would be drawn to her.<br /> <br /> <b>Wraith</b> \u2013 The woman who called herself the Wraith was the City\u2019s leading thief, able to enter and leave a location like a ghost. She was considered uncatchable by all, and even Greyfells and Lady Ashe had a difficult time trying to apprehend her, which they never did. She had the notoriety of being one of the few villains to never be caught from the pulp era, vanishing just after WW2 broke out. <br /> <br /> Emma Simone Mars was the daughter of a middle class family in the more affluent part of Old City. Having an older brother and sister and two younger brothers, she was the middle child and found herself generally left to her own devices. Suffering from a lack of attention and guidance, the family\u2019s nanny was concentrating on the younger siblings while the parents dotted on the older two, especially their son, she took to learning about the world on her own. She discovered very quickly that if she was unnoticed in what she did, she wouldn\u2019t call attention to herself and get into trouble or be told she couldn\u2019t do something. She took to practicing the art of being invisible in plain sight. She got good at it, very good, to the point where her family generally started to forget she was around. She had to remind them several times who she was at dinner when they\u2019d look at her strangely. When she reached the age where most of her contemporaries were being married off, she found that her art of being unseen in plain sight was doing the favor of not having to worry about being paired with some \u201cnitwit\u201d who she\u2019d have to sire a clump of children on. Using her considerable talents she carefully stole jewels, money, and other valuable items which she then sold through a fence. She made a name for herself as a thief of the highest caliber and soon found she was being sought out to do jobs, as no one expected the rather plain young proper woman to be a thief. Gathering her fortune she left home, completely unnoticed by her family, indeed when she went to visit them some years later they claimed they had no idea who she was and had her thrown out of their house. She returned the favor by robbing them blind of everything she could, all of them, from her parents, to her older and younger siblings, leaving them all bankrupt and destitute. <br /> <br /> Emma took to wearing dark clothing that hid her identify and due to her skills she was nicknamed the Wraith. When she manifested the ability to walk through walls, she literally became the ghost she was purporting to be. <br /> <br /> As the Wraith she made a fortune, setting herself up as upper middle class widower who had been left a fortune by her dead husband as her cover. She attended the right parties and events, making note of valuables and stealing when needed or contracted to do so. Nothing was above her prevue except violence. She refused to hurt someone physically. She took great care to make sure all her jobs were done quietly and without anyone seeing her, which only led to her gaining an even greater reputation.<br /> She came to light in the papers after being contracted to steal a piece of equipment from a lab. What she didn\u2019t know was that the person who hired her was the Aviator, an up and coming hero, and that the lab was her lab and the piece of equipment merely a lure. Working with Greyfells and Lady Ashe, the Aviator set up everything and waited. Sure enough the Wraith entered the location to take the item.<br /> <br /> The resulting chase across the city was seen by hundreds if not thousands, and was captured by cameras everywhere. The Wraith escaped, using her ability to pass through solid objects to finally go into the deep tunnels under the city, much to her pursuers ire, but the next day pictures of her, though in her costume and unidentifiable, were the front page of every paper. <br /> <br /> The resulting fallout did net her more jobs and suddenly she found herself being blamed for any unsolved theft in the city. Using her abilities she kept to the shadows and only took the choicest assignments, doing heavy amounts of research into the clients and the job through intermediaries so as to not reveal herself, and only finally doing the theft when she was sure it wasn\u2019t a setup. This didn\u2019t stop the Aviator and the Greyfellss from trying to stop her, but they were never successful. <br /> <br /> Emma had her biggest score just before the break out of World War 2, stealing a collection of gems that she sold on the black market for enough to retire on, which she promptly did, hiding away her outfit and deciding to live the rest of her life quietly.<br /> <br /> While she did on occasion pull a job here and there, for the most part she did as she intended. She cruised the parties, dallied with young men, contributed to charities, had tea with other members of the elite, rich and famous and lived the rest of her life in comfort till she died in her sleep of pneumonia on winter. Her entire fortune was amassed and given to her great-nephew, a relative who she\u2019d kept an eye on and had deemed was similar to her in nature, an ignored middle child. <br /> <br /> <i>The Shadows</i> \u2013 Emma was a master class thief who, thanks to telluric energies, had the ability to pass through solid matter for brief periods of time. This took a lot out of her and she would need to rest for a little before re-attempting it, so she used it sparingly and generally only in emergencies.<br /> <br /> <i>Appearance </i>\u2013 Emma was rather non-descript woman. Reddish brown hair, grey-green eyes, and an average look, she fit in in almost any crowd. She had a light, soft voice and was always polite and proper when in mixed company. She tended to dress conservatively in public, furthering her non-descript look and helping people forget about her.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/722-walksforever","name":"Walksforever","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar722_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"213"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-18T09:11:52-07:00","id":1397308,"title":"","content":"Couple more..<br /> <br /> <b>The Aviator</b> \u2013The pulp age of The City had many who heeded the call of adventure and fought crime in order to better the lot of the people. Some were lauded with praise and near worship, like Greyfells and Lady Ashe, others were seen with fear, like the Whisperer, and then there is the Aviator, who was seen with wonder. Clad head to toe in a flight suit and jacket with a full helmet ala something out of the rocketeer, the Aviator soared the skies of the city dealing out justice to those who broke the law. The roar of a jetpack and the sound of a sonic weapon heralded the arrival of the Aviator as he swopped down from the sky to catch the criminal. The police, while finding his antics rather wild and sensational, appreciated all the efforts he did as his unique perspective helped catch criminals who generally thought they\u2019d gotten away. Displayed on posters holding the American flag he was used as propaganda for tourism and to push patriotism, especially when WW2 broke out. The Aviator was considered a true hero, and many young boys wished they could be him. The crux was that the Aviator was not a him, but a her.<br /> <br /> Born to an inventor father and science teacher mother in the lower income part of Old City, Clarice Solomon was raised in a very untraditional un-lady like way for the 20s. Her parents fed her voracious appetite for learning everything they could, teaching her languages, science, history, politics and anything else they could get their hands on. Mocked and shunned at school, she spent her early years at home in her dad\u2019s lab inventing things with him, soon surpassing even his abilities. Known in their neighborhood as where you went to get something fixed, she was soon taking the junked and broken unwanted items and tinkering with them to learn how they worked. Her first jetpack woke the entire area when it launched and exploded, but she and her family were ecstatic. Refinement after refinement soon had the thing working like a charm and in secluded areas she would zip around, her father watching and monitoring while her mother made calculations for the future. The appearance of crime lords, the Greyfells and the Whisperer gave Clarice her idea. Aware that she would need an alter ego, she gathered the materials and fashioned herself the costume and helmet. With the aid of her father\u2019s van, the family drove out one night, and the Aviator was born. Since that day the three of them had formed a tight knit team, refining the equipment and suit, all the while making sure everyone thought that the Aviator was a man.<br /> <br /> Clarice had a successful career as a crime fighter, fast becoming a symbol that the City could use to push tourism and patriotism. Many wondered if the Aviator was an ex pilot and others wonder if the reason the helmet never came off was either because he was horribly disfigured or was a famous member of the City wanting to stay anonymous. Over the years before WW2 she managed to thwart The Jade Eye, King Thunder and almost caught the Wraith on several occasions. When WW2 broken out she retired, mainly because everyone would wonder why the Aviator had stayed and not gone overseas to fight in the war. Of course the disappearance of the flying hero made everyone guess that is exactly what happened. Clarice would have stayed retired if it hadn\u2019t been for family back in Europe, Germany to be exact. Hearing of members disappearing she took her gear, got passage to England, and sailed off. The papers carried news of the Aviator some weeks later, over Germany doing daring rescues of people from Nazi persecution.<br /> <br /> For the course of the war her family, and the City at large, read about the Aviator\u2019s adventures against the Nazis, fighting with several of the pulp age heroes against the minions of the Third Reich. When the war finally ended the Allies wanted to reward the Aviator, but Clarice had already slipped away, afraid to reveal who she really was. She returned to the City, and once again sought to retire. She had met someone while fighting in the war and now planned to get married and settle down. Her husband was Lt Col Roger White, also known as Defender, one of the Allied heroes who fought in the war. Moving to the City they settled down across the street from her parents for a quiet life.<br /> <br /> Life is never that easy though, and a year after their birth of their son, Victor, a crime wave rippled across the city as the cold war period became the norm and paranoia was high. With Greyfells off in Washington, the Whisperer vanished and Lady Ashe raising her children, the City seemed unprotected, till both Defender and the Aviator arrived on the scene. For three years the two would patrol the City, dealing with the remaining crime element that seemed to so large in the pulp era. Their last major act was when they brought the Gentleman\u2019s Gentleman to justice. They then put up their gloves for good and faded into stories, TV specials, and movies. <br /> <br /> In the years since they raised three children and became grandparents to 2 more. Roger died in 2003 and Clarice 2005, survived by their two sons and daughter and two granddaughters. <br /> <br /> <i>The shadows </i>\u2013 Clarice\u2019s was a genius when it came to inventing, able to blend telluric energy and tech to create items that should not have worked, like her jet pack and the sonic pistols she carried. During WW2 she created several items of the Allied heroes, especially Defender. All the items she created currently reside with her one granddaughter who is thinking of taking up the mantle.<br /> <br /> <i>Appearance</i> \u2013 Clarice was a tall, slender woman, with short dark hair. She was considered to be a classic beauty by those who knew her, both in looks and attitude and how she treated others. <br /> <br /> <b>The Gentleman\u2019s Gentleman</b> \u2013 Reginald George Somersby III. Reginald was born into a family that worked as butlers going back several generations. The men of the family had always been a gentleman\u2019s gentleman, providing butler/manservant services. Reginald entered the trade early, being trained by his father, but soon grew to find the job demeaning. As he watched his father serve, grovel and abase himself for a pair of rich elite snobs who could care less about him, he realized what he was doomed to be himself. He grew despondent and started to hatch a plan. He figure that since generations of his family has been basically slaves to the rich, it was time the rich paid their fair share to him, the last member of the family. He discovered very quickly that manservants became privy to all sorts of information, like who was sleeping with whom, and where the money was kept as well as the bodies sometimes. Using this knowledge he began to secretly siphon money from his employer till one day the family awoke to find they were broke and having to dismiss their servants never realizing the reason was right there. Reginald went from employer to employer, always making sure to get in good and trusted with all the right people and then slowly siphoning money. He was good at it as well, till he was found out by Lord Greyfells. <br /> <br /> Using the resources he\u2019d gathered he quickly avoided capture and went dark. Using his contacts he gathered like-minded people and created a small gang. Making sure to keep everything slow and quiet, he sent his people out to do what he had been doing. He managed to do this for another couple years before being caught and put in prison. Using his skills he endeared himself to the prison hierarchy quickly and was soon treated as an untouchable, with neither guards nor inmates wanting to hurt him. Indeed the heads of the prison gangs found his services almost irreplaceable and so did the guards as a go between. The prison ran so smoothly for the years he was in, that when he was release for good behavior the entire prison, staff and inmates almost rioted over him leaving. Of course while incarcerated he had continued to run his operations, using multiple middlemen who posed as his family and a young lady who posed as his wife to get messages out and back. Once he was out of prison he effortlessly took over operation again, this time aiming at making sure he\u2019d not get caught.<br /> <br /> Taking the name, the Gentleman\u2019s Gentleman, he smoothly ran his \u201cgang\u201d of butlers, maids, footman and other servants who would infiltrate various households and upper class establishments such as clubs, restaurants, and hotels where they would learn information on the clients and then use that information to fleece, blackmail and outright steal from them. Working as a valet to a wealthy business owner he ran his operations successfully till the outbreak of WW2. Drafted into service, he vanished in the D-Day invasion, and was reported MIA. The organization attempted to stay viable, but fell apart due to greed and infighting. An empty grave was commission in Old City veteran\u2019s cemetery by his wife to mark his passing.<br /> <br /> <i>The shadows</i> \u2013 The Gentleman\u2019s Gentleman was a good thief and an excellent strategic planner. He had no telluric enhanced abilities.<br /> <br /> <i>Appearance </i>\u2013 A robust and heavy set man, Reginald has thinning hair and the look of someone who had eaten maybe one too many pies. He had a constant smile and jovial laugh.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/722-walksforever","name":"Walksforever","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar722_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"213"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-19T20:28:10-07:00","id":1397616,"title":"","content":"And a couple more .. <br /> <br /> <b>The Whisperer</b> \u2013 No one is sure where the person known as the Whisperer came from. He appeared on the scene in 1929 one night, stopping a bank robbery. The robbers reported a man in black with a mask appearing out of nowhere, who beat them all within an inch of their lives before tying them up. They reported that whenever they were close to him there was the sound of whispers constantly, as if there were multiple people whispering around him. The police at first took little notice, as this vigilante was just another nut in a costume helping out, and who cared if a few criminals were hurt being brought to justice. Within a year though the police had changed their mind. Criminals with a few bruises was one thing, but dead bodies and survivors in a state of mind one could only label as insane, made for very bad press that the Whisperer was still out there \u201chelping\u201d.<br /> <br /> At first the police tried to just leave him messages, asking that he step it back a bit, not do so much damage, but it was like asking a thunderstorm not to rain hard. They next petitioned Lord Greyfells to see if perhaps could talk to the enigmatic vigilante. Greyfells attempted to talk some sense into the Whisperer but all he would say afterwards was that there was no answer to their problem. <br /> <br /> By 1932 the Whisperer had managed to interfere in multiple schemes of the Jade Eye, a crime lord in the little china district of Riverside. The two clashed regularly until the Jade Eye managed to get a massive manhunt declared on him through his contacts. The Whisperer managed to avoid police with ease, seeming to not care if he was located by any criminals, leaving those that attempted to apprehend him for the bounty either dead or wishing they were. Finally the issue came to a head and the Whisperer visited the Jade Eye on night for a conversation. What was said is unknown, and the only people other than the Whisperer and the Jade Eye who were privy to it evidently went mad according to rumors. The bounty was cancelled and the Whisperer vanished into the night and off the grid for almost six months.<br /> <br /> Little is known of this anti-hero\u2019s activities over the next few years. Police reports as well as information from Lord Greyfells show that he was active, foiling various low end crooks and occasionally stopping a major robbery or kidnapping. When Lord Greyfells and Lady A, along with the Aviator went up against a massive crime wave instigated by the Gentleman\u2019s Gentleman, he was there with them, appearing at strange times to lend a hand or deliver intelligence on the movements of those involved. Still little was known of who he was and where he was going to when he vanished. Many thought he was just a troubled homeless man who assumed the outfit when he had breakdowns. Others considered that perhaps he was one of the elite, trying to do his part while staying incognito. When WW2 broke out the Whisperer seemed to take up the slack that other heroes left when they became involved in the war. As the war years passed he became more and more involved in fighting crime and stopping the Jade Eye in particular. Finally the Jade Eye had enough and set a trap for him with the help of a hero hunter known as the Judge. <br /> <br /> Luring the Whisperer to the Breakwater Industrial Railyards, the three engaged in a brutal and short fight at the end of spring 1937. The Jade Eye managed to channel all his telluric energy into one massive strike and the resulting explosion killed the Judge and threw the Whisperer clear across the yards. The Jade Eye suffered a massive stroke at this point and also fell, the police arriving within the next half hour to discover his and the Judge\u2019s bodies. <br /> <br /> The Whisperer came to unsure who or where he was. He pulled the strange bandages from his body and wandered off into the night. Resting at a homeless shelter he was clothed and fed, but couldn\u2019t remember anything. For three months he wandered the streets, ranting to the voices in his head till he was picked up by the police and taken to the Kerrigan Asylum.<br /> The doctors at the asylum couldn\u2019t make heads or tails for what was causing the strange man\u2019s delusions, and so put him on an extreme regime of anti-psychotics, anti-depressants, and sedatives. They also administered intermittent shock therapy to try to get him right. Nothing worked. Eventually they just left him drugged to the gills, half-awake in a room, able to feed himself and use the toilet and that\u2019s about it. A doctor would occasionally come in and check on him for changes, but none were ever forthcoming. It was after ten years as a patient that they notice something. He wasn\u2019t aging. The doctors again engaged in a battery of testing on him, but still couldn\u2019t not find any reason for what was going on. The government caught wind, it was the height of the cold war at this time, and stepped in. The doctors who did the next set of examinations were none to gentle, and some of the tests were baseline torture and brutally invasive. Nothing yielded results. The government decided to leave him at the asylum under watch, returning to test him each year again. As time pass though, the tests became less frequent till twenty years later as the 70s came to a close he was just an unknown patient that was given food and drink along with a heavy regime of drugs each day and left alone. He became forgotten, a faceless nobody that the hospital would not admit they had, as who would believe them to start with and it would also cut off the money the government was feeding them to take care of the strange man.<br /> <br /> It was in 2008 when a sympathetic nurse, curious why he\u2019d never been allowed time outside in the gardens, lead him outside for the first time in almost seventy years. After a moment of staring at the sun, he turned to the young woman and in a completely lucid frame of mind, thanked her for freeing him and promptly vanished over the wall with a feat of superhuman speed and strength. The staff did not report this, as how can one report a 112 year old man who looks like he is 30 escaping the asylum. Considering the government hadn\u2019t visited in close the thirty years, they just left it as is, quietly sweeping it all under the carpet. <br /> <br /> It took a week for the first victims of the Whisperer to appear. A midnight bank job went south as a man in dark clothing wrapped in bandages dropped in out of the skylight to attack. The five men were quickly subdued and beaten within an inch of their lives by this strange man who seems to be surrounded by the whispers of a dozen people. The police filed their report, but since all files and records of the Whisperer have long since been lost, with only memorabilia of him at the Pulp Museum existing, they are at a loss of how to deal with this sudden vigilante. <br /> Over the last few years the Whisperer has appeared here and there, ruining plans of crooks and gangs as well as number of supernatural factions as he goes about his tasks, before vanishing into the night for months at a time. No one is sure where he goes or what he\u2019s doing, only that he now a serious player in an already crowded night.<br /> <br /> <i>The Shadows </i>\u2013 The Whisperer is gifted or perhaps cursed with the souls of those wanting justice and vengeance. They whisper to him all the time, causing him to talk to himself in multiple conversations. They also lend him their strength, stamina, speed and health, giving him incredible physical capabilities, preternatural speed and reaction and a nearly endless life through a form of complete cellular regeneration. He can take damage, and he feels it, but it heals almost instantly.<br /> <br /> <i>Appearance </i>\u2013 Most of the time all that is seen is a man in a dark long coat, with dark pants and boots, his entire upper body and head wrapping in loose flowing bandages. A wild, unkempt, bearded man of what looks like to be 30 is underneath it all.<br /> <br /> <b>The Judge</b> \u2013 Little is known about the person called the Judge. Not even Lord Greyfells\u2019s resources could find out any background material on this man who styled himself as a hero hunter. What little could be found showed that he first appeared on the scene in Miami, Florida as a bounty hunter, bringing in the hardest bounties available with a nearly 100% success rate. It is not known what caused him to change his tactics from bounty hunting criminals to working for them and hunting \u201cheroes\u201d but his first confirmed \u201cbounty\u201d was a vigilante known as Viking, who patrolled Miami bringing criminals to justice. After Viking, came the Scarlet Wind, another vigilante who had enhanced speed. Again the hero was captured and given over to the criminals that he was stopping. The Judge\u2019s trail of hero hunting slowly worked its way up the coast till it ended in New York where he spent nearly half a decade hunting the vigilantes and heroes of New York. He went quiet during World War 2, which lead Greyfells to believe he was drafted into the war. Post war the Judge re-appeared, again working for the criminals. His final job was when he was hired by the Jade Eye to deal with the Whisperer, as task that killed him, as his employer in the end. The Whisperer proved to be the greatest target the Judge had ever dealt with, as he never caught him and it was only through an elaborate trap, one that many thing was actually set by the Whisperer and not the Judge and the Jade Eye that he finally confronted his target. The battle that followed killed him. When he was taken to the morgue, he had no ID and his fingerprints were not on file, nor was there any record of him anywhere including military records. Greyfells posited in his memoirs that the Judge who came to the City was actually the second person to carry the name, the first having been drafted into the war and dying overseas. Greyfells theorized that it might have been the original\u2019s son carrying on the work. The Judge was buried in an unmarked grave next to the Jade Eye.<br /> <br /> <i>The Shadows</i> \u2013 The Judge was mortal, and had no telluric enhanced powers. He was an exceptional detective, and superb hunter. He was also an Olympic level athlete and could have easily boxed professionally. As a bounty hunter he was unmatched, always getting his man. He soon found out that the life of a bounty hunter was unrewarding. When he was offered a large sum of money to hunt down and bring a local vigilante to a local mob boss he found it exhilarating and switched careers. Greyfells\u2019s theory was correct about the war was partially correct. The Judge\u2019s son was drafted, not him, and he spent the war caring for his grandchildren full time till his son returned home.<br /> <br /> <i>Appearance </i>\u2013 The Judge was just over 6ft tall with a solid build one would expect in professional boxers and track stars. He had dark hair shot through with grey and a slightly crooked nose from an ill-healed break. When out on the \u201cjob\u201d he wore judge\u2019s robe with a hood and a black featureless mask with eye holes. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/722-walksforever","name":"Walksforever","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar722_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"213"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-20T11:32:40-07:00","id":1397777,"title":"","content":"These characters are really cool! I actually know a real life judge who was a boxer before he went to law school.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-20T12:22:23-07:00","id":1397789,"title":"","content":"I've a few more to post.. some WW2 heroes and villains then a modern day one.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/722-walksforever","name":"Walksforever","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar722_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"213"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-22T16:32:57-07:00","id":1398254,"title":"","content":"Some of the WW2 heroes and villains. Caution .. the bad guys are bad guys .. they did horrible things .. they are meant to be pulp style horror bad guy nazis .. I apologize now if they offend anyone. <br /> <br /> <b>WW2 (1939-1945)</b><br /> <b>Defender </b>\u2013 Roger Decker was an all American athletic and scholar. He came from an impoverished family, but strived in class and on the field to make something of himself. He graduated from high school top of his class as well as being captain of the football team. He got into West Point and graduated in 1922, the year the Telluric wave occurred. While celebrating his graduation he experienced his first abilities. He went to this superiors and reported it. Aware of the situation and what had caused it, the DoD sent him to a special research base when, along with top trainers, scientists and equipment, Defender was born. <br /> <br /> <b>Sunstrike \u2013 </b>Japan has its own hero during the war, a master strategist, martial artist and natural leader with enhanced speed and the ability to channel his ki into lethal strikes which caused a flash of yellow-white light, hence his name. Col. Togawa Hiyuki served faithfully and was killed trying to save people from Hiroshima when the bomb exploded. <br /> <br /> <b>Britannia \u2013 </b>Capt. Jack Barrows, known as Britannia, was one of the group of Allied heroes that fought against the Axis Four and the Blitzwolfe. Dark haired with a quick wit and a face that women fell in love with with but one look, Britannia was the UKs premier hero. Gifted with strength, speed, and endurance far surpassing even Olympic athletes, he was in the forefront of dozens of battles alongside Defender, The Tank, and the Aviator against the Axis. Barrows retired after the war to Yorkshire where is was reported he lived till 102, a consummate bachelor his entire life.<br /> <br /> <b>The Tank \u2013 T</b>he Russian Living Weapon, as he was known, Alexi Yuri Bogdanovich was the only child of two farmers from one of the western farming enclaves. A massive man, looking like the stereotypical strong man from carnivals, Alexi was a gentle giant who only used his abilities to defend the weak a, innocent and abused. A local hero, he was personally recruited to fight the Axis by Stalin, given the rank of staff sergeant, and sent to join the Allied heroes on the front. Alexi was often called the glue of the team, acting as an advisor and friend to all, as well as their tactician. It was on his advice that the Aviator revealed herself to the group, having figured out she was a woman the day they met. Alexi\u2019s most notable feat during the war was when he made a final stand against the Blitzwolfe, a squad of uratha SS who had come to kill the Allied heroes. Few really knew the extent of Alexi\u2019s abilities, not even himself, but on that day, in that town, Alexi not only engaged the squad solo, but proceeded to kill every single one of them with his bare hands. He was found by The Aviator in the wrecked town\u2019s center, surrounded by the bodies of the Blitzwolfe, regenerating from his wounds. Sadly the encounter had snapped Alexi\u2019s mind, driving him into a deep catatonia. He was returned to his parent\u2019s farm, awarded the Order of Lenin and Hero of the Soviet Union and left to live out his life in the care of his family. Alexi never fully recovered, only have brief periods of lucidity, spending the remaining years of his life sitting in a chair watching the seasons pass, able to only do very basic life functions. He died in 1965 and was buried on his family\u2019s farm. The Aviator snuck into the USSR to attended the funeral. Alexi was supernaturally strong, able to life a tractor above his head with ease. He was also basically invulnerable, able to regenerate from nearly any wound almost instantly, add to this that he was incredibly tough, basically bullet proof, his name made sense. Alexi was also highly intelligent, with a mind for strategy and tactics, and loved playing chess with anyone.<br /> <br /> <b>The Axis Four</b> \u2013 the Axis Four were the Nazi\u2019s answer to the Allied heroes that started appearing in the war. The first was Iron Eagle, with his Blitzwolfe SS squad of werewolves. Then Annihilator and Scythe appeared on the scene and finally Ghost Legion. The Axis Four and the Bitzwolfe were a formidable group and caused immense loss of life and property to the Allies before they were stopped. Unknown to the Allies, the Axis Four were rife with infighting and hatred for each other.<br /> <br /> <b>Iron Eagle</b> \u2013 Oberstleutnant Johan Krieg grew up fully committed to the ideal of Nazi Germany. Coming from a rich family with a long history of military service he was already an up and coming officer in the newly created German army when the call went out for volunteers for a special program. He volunteered and, along with two hundred others, subjected to a process where telluric energy was bombarded into his body in a special chamber. Only he and three others stepped survived. Deemed a failed program by high command for creating super humans, Krieg and the other survivors were further trained to use their new found abilities. For Krieg this came naturally. His newly gained strength, speed, reflexes, coordination and endurance along with his classic blonde Nordic looks, made his the poster child for the Nazi ideal. Code named Iron Eagle, he became the leader of the Axis Four, a position he constantly made sure the other three members were always aware of, especially Annihilator, who also desired command and constantly questioned Krieg\u2019s orders and command decisions. Krieg didn\u2019t trust Ghost Legion, seeing magic as unnatural, especially magic that dealt with the dead. Scythe he found compellingly attractive, and the fact she was with Annihilator didn\u2019t stop him from taking her for himself several times, threatening to have her lover arrested and given to the science labs to be dissected for research if she didn\u2019t keep quiet about it. Krieg was promoted several times due his teams successes, all which he contributed to his leadership, not that he wasn\u2019t a gifted and charismatic leader as well as a talented officer when it came to strategy and tactics, but often his ego lead the way. He was given command of the Blitzwolfe squad after beating one of them in hand to hand combat. Krieg survived the war, hiding out in the ruins of Berlin when the Allies and Russia invaded. He managed to stage a number of terror attacks before meeting his death at the hands of Scythe who had defected to the Allies once news of Hitler\u2019s death was reported. Left for the dogs by Scythe he was raised by Ghost Legion, becoming a bound zombie slave to the necromancer.<br /> <br /> <b>Annihilator \u2013</b> Hauptmann Karl Meier was drafted into the army at the age of 18, and a year later volunteered for the super solider program the Wunderwaffen were running. One of the four survivors, Karl would have went over the edge insane if it hadn\u2019t been for Dagmar Ahlbrecht. The two bonded over the experience, becoming lovers. Their similar abilities had the two train to become assassins, with Karl an expert in close combat and weapons and Dagmar with ranged weapons. Karl\u2019s exposure to the telluric energies had enhanced his reflexes and speed, making his blindingly fast. Karl and Dagmar often worked as a team, sent deep into Allied territory to assassinate targets of importance. Several times they ran afoul of the Allied heroes. Karl fancied himself a leader, and while he was a competent officer, his command skills were more in his own head than real, but he was constantly sure his ideas were the best, which caused continual friction between him and Johan. Add to the mix that he could see Johan looking at Dagmar all the time made him quiet jealous as well. Karl was killed in the final days of the attack on Berlin by Johan. When the news broke that Hitler was dead, Johan and Dagmar decided to surrender to the allies. Krieg found out and managed to catch up with them as they fled. Karl confronted Krieg while Dagmar fled, and was killed in the confrontation. Sadly the last thing Karl heard was Krieg telling him of all the times he had raped Dagmar.<br /> <br /> <b>Ghost Legion \u2013</b> Oberleutnant Jens von Hauser. The von Hauser family has had links into the supernatural parts of the world for hundreds of years. Their lineage includes several hedge mages, a couple \u201cwitches\u201d, a Bound or two and even a mage if the family stories are to be believed. All members are known to have some talent in some form or another. Jens was the exception. Ostrazied by his family he joined the Luftwaffe and became a pilot. His skills were mediocre and earned him several reprimands and finally he was \u201cvolunteered\u201d for the super soldier experiment. Jens swears he didn\u2019t survive the process, yet there he stood with the other three in the end. A short, somewhat thin man, the process caused him to become near skeletal in appearance. The most surprising thing was he could see the dead. Spirits surrounded him and if he concentrated he could summon them to do his bidding, either in the dead bodies of the fallen or as hazy ghosts. Jens was most ignored by the other three. Krieg found him repulsive, and Karl and Dagmar found him frightening and cold. Jens spent most of his time perfecting his abilities, managing to at one point to bring almost fifty dead to bear against the Allies in one battle, and when one of his dead was destroyed he\u2019d just pull up another. With the fall of the Reich Jens decided to flee the country, assured that the Allies would likely kill him if he surrendered. By chance he found Krieg\u2019s body as he was leaving the city, gutted by Dagmar and left for the dogs. Using his power he pulled Krieg back to life and bound him to him to be his bodyguard. The two vanished into the night and history.<br /> <br /> <b>Scythe \u2013</b> Oberleutnant Dagmar Ahlbrecht was the ideal of what the Reich wanted. Tall, athletic, blonde, blue eyed, intelligent and driven by the idea of what the Reich was and stood for. She was recruited at an early age into the propaganda corps, and quickly became their poster child, often see in pictures and movies where they needed advertise the Reich as the perfect place to be. It was pure chance that had he assigned to the super solider program. Part of the film crew that was there to record the heroic volunteers, she became accidently trapped in one of the chambers during a shoot. The mechanism auto started and bombarded her with telluric energy. When she awoke she was in a hospital and could only hear the sobs of the man in the bed next to her. She started talking to him, learning his name and then sharing her life and experiences with him. That day she saved Karl and forged a love that would carry the two of them through the war. Already a crack shot, trained to make the films even more realistic, the energies had hyper accelerated her senses giving her hyperkinesis, which allowed her brain to process movement at a much faster rate than others. This gave her amazing athletic feats of timing, superhuman reflexes and perfect accuracy with firearms or thrown objects and also allowed her, for example, to predict trajectory by eyesight. She and Karl became assassins for the Reich, part of the Axis Four. From day one she realized that Krieg wanted her, but she was committed to Karl. When he forced himself on her she threatened to go to their superiors, but was laughed at and told by Krieg if she valued her lovers life she\u2019s endure his affections. Over the course of the war she slowly learned what the Reich was truly like, with the death camps, book burning, and master plan for the master race and so on. She and Karl soon realized that they needed to stop this. She started feeding intel to the Allies, making drops here and there. When D-Day happened she made sure she fed as much intel to them as possible on troop movements in order to accelerate the fall of the Reich. She even got Karl involved, especially when her contact in the Allies promised her and Karl amnesty if they defected. When the Allies seiged Berlin and the news of Hitler\u2019s death was reported the two fled for the Allied lines. Krieg chased after them and had it not been for the sacrifice of Karl she would have been killed. Making it to the Allied lines she was found by The Aviator who got prepared to fly her to safety, only to be convinced to fly back to find Karl. They found his corpse and in the distance saw Krieg running. Getting the Aviator to lift her in the air she sighted down her custom sniper and fired her last shot of the war, smiling as she saw it blow through Krieg\u2019s chest. Dagmar spent three years after the war in the UK as a guest of British Intelligence before being released. She returned to Berlin and took up the cause of helping people flee from East Germany. She was killed in 1975 by members of the Stasi as she was helping two families across the wall.<br /> <br /> <b>The Blitzwolfe </b>\u2013 The Pure tribes of the Uratha saw the Reich as a means to an end. Members of the Predator Kings, Ivory Claws and Fire Touched all happily joined the Reich in its goals usually working in the shadows. A small team of them though approached the Thule Society through a third party and offered the service as a squad of hunters for the Reich. After intense negotations, the Blitzwolfe SS detachment was entered into the records. A true black ops wet work group, the Blitzwolfe committed acts of violence, barbarity, terror, and outright slaughter in the Fuhrer\u2019s name during the course of the war. Their missions became tales of horror for the Allies and even for those of the Reich. The squad met their end when they were assigned to wipe out a town that was near the Allies push, in order to deny its supplies and man power to the Allies. As they entered the town they found it empty except for a large Russian man known as The Tank, who stood in the town center. Issuing a challenge to open combat he charged the uratha. To say they were surprised was an understand, but it paled in comparison when The Tank didn\u2019t react to their changing to their war forms, and it wasn\u2019t till he\u2019d torn two of them apart with his bare hands that they realized that he was far more than human. Slain to the last, the final member of the Blitzwolfe attempted to flee only to be gripped in a bear hug that crushed his entire upper body before being ripped in half.<br /> <br /> <b>Post WW2 (1945-1955)</b><br /> <b>Ravager \u2013 </b>No one is quite sure who Ravager was, only that he came to \u201clight\u201d in post war East Berlin, hunting vampires. Dozens of neonates and fledglings died under his hands before the local prince exerted his influence and got the Stasi to hunt down the hero. No one was found and the killing stop for a couple years. Then the Ravager reappeared, his victims destroyed by fire or in the light of the sun. The Stasi finally caught the Ravager in a warehouse and gunned him down. The person under the mask was an unknown man, who merely told the Stasi \u201cthere is always a Ravager\u201d before dying.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/722-walksforever","name":"Walksforever","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar722_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"213"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-24T05:53:45-07:00","id":1398587,"title":"","content":"Last one .. a modern day hero.<br /> <br /> <b>The Modern era</b><br /> <b>Stormcaller</b> \u2013 There has been a surge in costumed heroes appearing on the streets again, playing vigilante in places where they think there is no help being provided by police. Most often these so called heroes run afoul of the gangs they are trying to scare and end up dead in an alley and a foot note in some detective and mortician\u2019s report. Some survive for a while, but invariably with the way the world is in the Chronicles of Darkness, unless they possess some sort of supernatural power, they are contending with not only normal criminals but also possibly their supernatural masters, pawns and servants, not to mention random things that go bump in the night and sometimes like to snack on the unwary.<br /> <br /> Every once in a while a hero appears, one who can actually stand their own against the night and help to an extent. Again these people tend to last about as long as it takes to piss off a powerful vampire, werewolf, or possibly a mage or worse. If they are lucky they hang up the spandex and walk (maybe limp or wheel) their way to what might be a normal life. If they are unlucky they might end up dead, or worse, like Stonefist, a strength enhanced hero who went from normal criminals to vampire hunting. He vanished one night, only to reappear two weeks later a mindless, blood addicted, ghoul slave doing the orders of the local vampire lord.<br /> <br /> Then there are the true heroes. Ones who embody the ideals of old and who able to stand their own against the night and the things out there in the night. They are rare in these modern nights but they do exist. Stormcaller is one such individual. <br /> <br /> She burst on to the scene one night when the police arrived at a nasty hostage situation with a local gang holed up in a residence. Officers reported seeing what looked like lightning ripple across the ground and then there was woman dressed in tight black, blue and white spandex standing on the roof. Moments later she vanished into the house. Within ten minutes the hostages were coming out the front door and when the police went in they found the gang members beaten unconscious. The hostages reported seeing the woman moving almost faster than the eye could see, blue-white lightning wreathing her body as she effortless took out all the gang members. <br /> <br /> In the weeks following a number of the local gangs had run-ins with her, usually to their detriment. The police were all too happy to collect her left overs, though the gangs lawyers screamed and argued vigilante justice and due process to get their clients back on the street, where they would just run into Stormcaller again. A number of the gang members went straight after a second run in, which caused concern for the gangs which were losing power and money. Of course this went up the food chain to their bosses. In one case it put a Forsaken Ghost Wolf on her trail. When he caught up with her, he was wary but figured he could handle it. She nearly beat him to death even with his abilities and powers. This of course sent waves through the supernatural underworld. Three Kindred decided she would make good sport and so went after her. All three were ash within a week.<br /> <br /> Stormcaller has been active now for almost two years, popping up and causing damage to various gangs, the mob, yakuza and triad groups as well as any supernaturals that prey on humans and their pawns and minions. She has proven to be the match for everything she has gone up against. In the current nights when she seen, most take that as a sign to be scarce.<br /> <br /> <i>The Shadows </i>\u2013 Stormcaller\u2019s real name is Alicia Simone Greyfells. She is lord Greyfells\u2019s great granddaughter. Stormcaller is one of a new breed, a person known as a Nova to those of the FEAR Corporation. Harnessing quantum energy she is able to manipulate energy about herself, covering herself in a field of lightning that can deal stun to lethal damage to anything she wants. The energy also gives her enhanced strength, speed, stamina, and senses, not to mention limited flight and an incredible healing ability. With all her power active, she can go toe to toe with a pack of Forsaken and win, which she has done. Her quantum powers also act as a null field towards most magic, meaning awakened find it difficult to target her with anything directly, and considering the fact she\u2019s basically supergirl covered in lightning, the non-direct stuff tends to not bother her much.<br /> <br /> This all comes with a price. She is aging rapidly. Under the high tech bullet proof costume is a late 30s women who looks like she is in her late 40s. She is currently aging at 2x the normal rate and her own research shows that it will increase in factor every couple years. In ten years it will 5x normal speed, 5 days for each 1 that passes.<br /> <br /> <i>Appearance </i>\u2013 An athletic woman in her late 40s with dark red hair. Attractive and good natured, she always seems to be the life of the party and people seem to gravitate to her and her good attitude, mood and nature. When in persona, she is quiet and somber. Her costume covers her entire body leaving no indication of who she is other than a woman.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/722-walksforever","name":"Walksforever","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar722_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"213"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-25T13:53:39-07:00","id":1398868,"title":"","content":"So that's all I've got at this time for that slice of the City's history and a brief foray into Adventure!... I am hoping we get a Adventure! sourcebook for Continuum. I liked it. I used to play Daredevils and it was a nice homage and fun to run.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/722-walksforever","name":"Walksforever","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar722_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"213"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}